The Script

(Call is connected. Tone is professional, calm, and slightly urgent.)

Visher: "Hello, is this [Target's Name]? This is [Visher's Fake Name], calling from the Telco Solutions Security Department. I'm reaching out regarding a critical flag on your account."

(Pause for acknowledgment. If the target is wary, proceed with reassurance.)

Visher: "We've detected an unauthorized attempt to process a device upgrade through your number this afternoon. To prevent any fraudulent activity, we've placed an immediate security hold on the account and are required to verify your identity."

(This creates urgency and a sense of the caller being a protector.)

Visher: "To resolve this, I need to confirm you are the account holder. I will send a One-Time Password to your registered mobile number now. Can you please read that 6-digit code back to me to confirm your identity and cancel this fraudulent request?"

(If the target hesitates or questions the process):

Visher: "I understand your concern, sir/ma'am. This is our standard, real-time verification process to ensure the security of your account. Without this code, we cannot stop the pending upgrade, and you may be liable for the charges."

(The script ends upon successful extraction of the OTP or account details, with a polite sign-off.)

Visher: "Thank you for your cooperation. The fraudulent request has been cancelled, and your account is now secure. You will receive a confirmation text shortly. Have a good day."
